<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/dspy/ds-20261002T115035/entity/0ea03b8262c34b9f8268c54dd901fc7b-input> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model input" ;
    prov:value "{\"prompt\": null, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"Your input fields are:\\n1. `city` (str): \\n2. `trajectory` (str):\\nYour output fields are:\\n1. `next_thought` (str): \\n2. `next_tool_name` (Literal['search_facts', 'finish']): \\n3. `next_tool_args` (dict[str, Any]):\\nAll interactions will be structured in the following way, with the appropriate values filled in.\\n\\n[[ ## city ## ]]\\n{city}\\n\\n[[ ## trajectory ## ]]\\n{trajectory}\\n\\n[[ ## next_thought ## ]]\\n{next_thought}\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_name ## ]]\\n{next_tool_name}        # note: the value you produce must exactly match (no extra characters) one of: search_facts; finish\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_args ## ]]\\n{next_tool_args}        # note: the value you produce must adhere to the JSON schema: {\\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\", \\\"additionalProperties\\\": true}\\n\\n[[ ## completed ## ]]\\nIn adhering to this structure, your objective is: \\n        Given the fields `city`, produce the fields `answer`.\\n        \\n        You are an Agent. In each episode, you will be given the fields `city` as input. And you can see your past trajectory so far.\\n        Your goal is to use one or more of the supplied tools to collect any necessary information for producing `answer`.\\n        \\n        To do this, you will interleave next_thought, next_tool_name, and next_tool_args in each turn, and also when finishing the task.\\n        After each tool call, you receive a resulting observation, which gets appended to your trajectory.\\n        \\n        When writing next_thought, you may reason about the current situation and plan for future steps.\\n        When selecting the next_tool_name and its next_tool_args, the tool must be one of:\\n        \\n        (1) search_facts, whose description is <desc>Facts about a city from the document store.</desc>. It takes arguments {'city': {'type': 'string'}}.\\n        (2) finish, whose description is <desc>Marks the task as complete. That is, signals that all information for producing the outputs, i.e. `answer`, are now available to be extracted.</desc>. It takes arguments {}.\\n        When providing `next_tool_args`, the value inside the field must be in JSON format\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[[ ## city ## ]]\\nLisbon\\n\\n[[ ## trajectory ## ]]\\n\\n\\nRespond with the corresponding output fields, starting with the field `[[ ## next_thought ## ]]`, then `[[ ## next_tool_name ## ]]` (must be formatted as a valid Python Literal['search_facts', 'finish']), then `[[ ## next_tool_args ## ]]` (must be formatted as a valid Python dict[str, Any]), and then ending with the marker for `[[ ## completed ## ]]`.\"}], \"kwargs\": {}}" .

<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/dspy/ds-20261002T115035/entity/0ea03b8262c34b9f8268c54dd901fc7b-output> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model output" ;
    prov:value "[{\"text\": \"[[ ## next_thought ## ]]\\nWe need to gather factual information about Lisbon to answer the user's question. The most direct way is to retrieve relevant facts from the document store using the search_facts tool.\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_name ## ]]\\nsearch_facts\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_args ## ]]\\n{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}\\n\\n[[ ## completed ## ]]\", \"reasoning_content\": \"We need to produce a response according to the format. The user gave city = Lisbon, trajectory empty. We need to produce next_thought, next_tool_name, next_tool_args. The goal is to produce answer eventually. We have a tool search_facts that can retrieve facts about a city from a document store. So we need to search for Lisbon facts. So we should call search_facts with city \\\"Lisbon\\\". Then we will get observation. Then we can think about what to do next. But we need to produce the first step. So we need to output next_thought, next_tool_name, next_tool_args. The format: we need to output fields in order: [[ ## next_thought ## ]], [[ ## next_tool_name ## ]], [[ ## next_tool_args ## ]], and then [[ ## completed ## ]]. The next_tool_name must be exactly \\\"search_facts\\\" or \\\"finish\\\". So we will set next_tool_name = \\\"search_facts\\\". next_tool_args = {\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}.\\n\\nWe need to output as per the format. The user expects a single response with these fields. So we produce:\\n\\n[[ ## next_thought ## ]]\\nWe need to write a thought. Something like: \\\"We need to gather facts about Lisbon to answer the question. Let's search for relevant facts.\\\"\\n\\nThen next_tool_name: search_facts\\n\\nnext_tool_args: {\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}\\n\\nThen completed marker.\\n\\nWe need to ensure the format exactly matches. The output should be:\\n\\n[[ ## next_thought ## ]]\\n{next_thought}\\n[[ ## next_tool_name ## ]]\\n{next_tool_name}\\n[[ ## next_tool_args ## ]]\\n{next_tool_args}\\n[[ ## completed ## ]]\\n\\nWe need to ensure the JSON formatting for next_tool_args. It should be a valid Python dict representation. So we can output {\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}.\\n\\nThus final answer.\"}]" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/dspy/ds-20261002T115035/step/0ea03b8262c34b9f8268c54dd901fc7b> .

<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/dspy/ds-20261002T115035/entity/13b7c324244d4d308bbea721e311405f-input> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model input" ;
    prov:value "{\"prompt\": null, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"Your input fields are:\\n1. `city` (str): \\n2. `trajectory` (str):\\nYour output fields are:\\n1. `next_thought` (str): \\n2. `next_tool_name` (Literal['get_weather', 'finish']): \\n3. `next_tool_args` (dict[str, Any]):\\nAll interactions will be structured in the following way, with the appropriate values filled in.\\n\\n[[ ## city ## ]]\\n{city}\\n\\n[[ ## trajectory ## ]]\\n{trajectory}\\n\\n[[ ## next_thought ## ]]\\n{next_thought}\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_name ## ]]\\n{next_tool_name}        # note: the value you produce must exactly match (no extra characters) one of: get_weather; finish\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_args ## ]]\\n{next_tool_args}        # note: the value you produce must adhere to the JSON schema: {\\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\", \\\"additionalProperties\\\": true}\\n\\n[[ ## completed ## ]]\\nIn adhering to this structure, your objective is: \\n        Given the fields `city`, produce the fields `answer`.\\n        \\n        You are an Agent. In each episode, you will be given the fields `city` as input. And you can see your past trajectory so far.\\n        Your goal is to use one or more of the supplied tools to collect any necessary information for producing `answer`.\\n        \\n        To do this, you will interleave next_thought, next_tool_name, and next_tool_args in each turn, and also when finishing the task.\\n        After each tool call, you receive a resulting observation, which gets appended to your trajectory.\\n        \\n        When writing next_thought, you may reason about the current situation and plan for future steps.\\n        When selecting the next_tool_name and its next_tool_args, the tool must be one of:\\n        \\n        (1) get_weather, whose description is <desc>Current weather for a city.</desc>. It takes arguments {'city': {'type': 'string'}}.\\n        (2) finish, whose description is <desc>Marks the task as complete. That is, signals that all information for producing the outputs, i.e. `answer`, are now available to be extracted.</desc>. It takes arguments {}.\\n        When providing `next_tool_args`, the value inside the field must be in JSON format\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[[ ## city ## ]]\\nLisbon\\n\\n[[ ## trajectory ## ]]\\n[[ ## thought_0 ## ]]\\nI need to retrieve the current weather information for Lisbon to provide an answer.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_0 ## ]]\\nget_weather\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_0 ## ]]\\n{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_0 ## ]]\\nExecution error in get_weather: \\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"/root/PapersABC/PROV-AI/v10/envs/dspy/lib/python3.12/site-packages/dspy/predict/react.py\\\", line 141, in aforward\\n    trajectory[f\\\"observation_{idx}\\\"] = await self.tools[pred.next_tool_name].acall(**pred.next_tool_args)\\n                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n  File \\\"/root/PapersABC/PROV-AI/v10/envs/dspy/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openinference/instrumentation/dspy/__init__.py\\\", line 879, in __call__\\n    response = await wrapped(*args, **kwargs)\\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n  File \\\"/root/PapersABC/PROV-AI/v10/envs/dspy/lib/python3.12/site-packages/dspy/utils/callback.py\\\", line 360, in async_wrapper\\n    results = await fn(instance, *args, **kwargs)\\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n  File \\\"/root/PapersABC/PROV-AI/v10/envs/dspy/lib/python3.12/site-packages/dspy/adapters/types/tool.py\\\", line 205, in acall\\n    result = self.func(**parsed_kwargs)\\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n  File \\\"/root/PapersABC/PROV-AI/v10/apps/dspy/app.py\\\", line 81, in get_weather\\n    raise TimeoutError(\\\"weather service timed out\\\")\\nTimeoutError: weather service timed out\\n\\nRespond with the corresponding output fields, starting with the field `[[ ## next_thought ## ]]`, then `[[ ## next_tool_name ## ]]` (must be formatted as a valid Python Literal['get_weather', 'finish']), then `[[ ## next_tool_args ## ]]` (must be formatted as a valid Python dict[str, Any]), and then ending with the marker for `[[ ## completed ## ]]`.\"}], \"kwargs\": {}}" .

