 next_tool_name, next_tool_args. There's no answer field. Possibly the answer is to be included in the final output after we call finish? The system says \\\"When finishing the task, you must output the following fields: ... and then ending with the marker for `[[ ## completed ## ]]`.\\\" It doesn't mention answer. So maybe the answer is not required to be output in this format; it's just internal. But the instructions say \\\"Given the fields `city`, produce the fields `answer`.\\\" That seems contradictory.\\n\\nWe need to interpret the meta-instructions. The user says: \\\"Your input fields are: 1. city (str): 2. trajectory (str): Your output fields are: 1. next_thought (str): 2. next_tool_name (Literal['search_facts', 'finish']): 3. next_tool_args (dict[str, Any]): All interactions will be structured in the following way, with the appropriate values filled in. ... In adhering to this structure, your objective is: Given the fields `city`, produce the fields `answer`. You are an Agent. In each episode, you will be given the fields `city` as input. And you can see your past trajectory so far. Your goal is to use one or more of the supplied tools to collect any necessary information for producing `answer`.\\\"\\n\\nThus, the answer is presumably something we need to produce, but the output format doesn't include answer. Possibly the answer is to be included in the final output after we call finish? But the finish tool description says \\\"Marks the task as complete. That is, signals that all information for producing the outputs, i.e. `answer`, are now available to be extracted.\\\" So after we call finish, the system will extract answer from the facts we have. So we just need to call finish now, because we have the fact about Lisbon. So we should output next_thought, next_tool_name = finish, next_tool_args = {}. Then completed marker.\\n\\nThus, we need to produce:\\n\\n[[ ## next_thought ## ]]\\n... reasoning that we have enough info.\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_name ## ]]\\nfinish\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_args ## ]]\\n{}\\n\\n[[ ## completed ## ]]\\n\\nWe need to ensure formatting exactly as described. The next_tool_name must be exactly \\\"finish\\\". The next_tool_args must be a JSON dict {}.\\n\\nThus, final answer.\"}]" ;
